+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys live in the data
+as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one per role.
+
+- `viewer` may read (every `GET` except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook` may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key whose role
+may not use the route answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that may change data (any method but `GET`) made with a known
+key writes an audit entry `{ at, keyName, method, path, status }`, also when
+it is refused or fails (a failed request's changes are rolled back).
+`GET /audit` lists the entries newest first.
+
